[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://scenes/props/socket_receptacle.tscn" id="3_receptacle"]

; A wall-mounted socket you plug a cable into (look + E). Mount with +Z into the room (its -Z is the
; wall side).
;
; MOUNT DISTANCE: the receptacle's back plate sits ON this node's origin, so the origin belongs on
; the wall's inner FACE plus a hair. RoomBuilder puts that face wall_thickness/2 = 0.075 m in from
; the wall line, so mount at ~0.095 — NOT at the 0.17 m the repair panels use (their housing is
; centred, so it needs the extra room), which leaves the socket floating visibly off the wall.
; Do not mount at exactly 0.075 either: the back plate then sits coplanar with the wall face and
; the two z-fight. The ~0.02 m of daylight is what stops that. `is_power_source` makes it a live outlet; leave it off for a device inlet. The
; StaticBody box lets the camera ray hit the faceplate; a seated plug is excepted from it.

